sition":{"commit_sha":"72be7960450ff04a9721920f362a3ce0bf809808","position":"1788037389975057001-f6d32cef-ac77-41d7-b838-9adc00a4f34a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1f67aecef8822d451ae72c0d08d230d96b93f0b57d08ca56ca1af9887615b89b","event_uuid":"7569a4e5-dc51-48f5-b3ad-4332d0ee0b83","position":{"commit_sha":"72be7960450ff04a9721920f362a3ce0bf809808","position":"1788037391565276001-7569a4e5-dc51-48f5-b3ad-4332d0ee0b83"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9cdde8ab798744bbbbbf55eb5187fbd0985bf2bba059854c7ab59de29d6257de","event_uuid":"2f0696e2-6293-4ad8-9a3f-407eb435be13","position":{"commit_sha":"8b701cea743eae14c89a037122cff7511e97bfe5","position":"1788037527999641001-2f0696e2-6293-4ad8-9a3f-407eb435be13"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix committed (3dcbed5aad6f) and pushed to Gerrit: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2387. Local gates verified: make lint, make typecheck, and pytest tests/unit/test_release_guards.py tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py (44 passed) all clean. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1788037527999641001}],"created_at":1788036299606306001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2a05427e-b6c4-476c-bfa3-d13f97a1bbfa","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c066-c496-7012-4a39"}],"description":"## Context\nDuring the 0.13.0 release (ticket hyperbolic-pernicious-drongo, Gerrit change 2385 merged as\n4dafd36d2aa1), release.yml's \"Publish to MCP Registry\" job failed all 5 retry attempts with:\n\n    Error: publish failed: server returned status 422: {\"title\":\"Unprocessable Entity\",\"status\":422,\n    \"detail\":\"validation failed\",\"errors\":[{\"message\":\"expected length <= 100\",\n    \"location\":\"body.description\",\"value\":\"Rebar can block work until an AI plan review passes,\n    require signed completion verification before close, and reconcile its event-sourced ticket\n    record with Jira across CLI, Python, and MCP.\"}]}\n\nserver.json's top-level \"description\" field (190 chars, identical to pyproject.toml's description)\nexceeds the registry's <= 100 char schema constraint. PyPI publish and the GitHub Release both\nsucceeded (irreversible, already live for 0.13.0); only the MCP Registry publish step failed.\nNothing in local CI (make lint, scripts/check_server_manifest.py, release_guards.py) catches this\nlocally -- the 422 was only ever surfaced by the live registry's remote validation during the\nrelease, after PyPI was already published.\n\n## Plan\n- Shorten server.json's top-level description to <= 100 chars (keep pyproject.toml's longer,\n  descriptive form -- there is no lockstep guard requiring the two to match, confirmed by\n  inspection of scripts/release_guards.py and scripts/check_server_manifest.py).\n- Add a local guard (check_mcp_registry_description function + a \"mcp-registry-description\" CLI\n  subcommand in scripts/release_guards.py, alongside the existing check_version_lockstep /\n  check_env_protection helpers) asserting server.json's top-level description is <= 100 chars,\n  with a unit test in tests/unit/test_release_guards.py.\n- WIRE the new guard into release.yml's \"Authorize release source\" job (a new \"Guard — server.json\n  description fits the MCP Registry schema\" step, immediately after the existing version-lockstep\n  guard step) so a future release fails BEFORE PyPI publish (irreversible) rather than only at the\n  live registry's remote validation after publish. This wiring is IN scope for this ticket -- the\n  guard function must have a real runner, not just unit-test coverage.\n- Attest (as a ticket comment, once the fix lands) the run URL/timestamp of the successful re-run\n  of release.yml run 33273822041's \"Publish to MCP Registry\" job -- this is an external,\n  point-in-time confirmation and is recorded as evidence, not a codebase acceptance criterion.\n\n## File impact\n- server.json — shorten top-level description field to satisfy the MCP registry's <= 100 char schema\n- scripts/release_guards.py — add check_mcp_registry_description guard + CLI subcommand\n- tests/unit/test_release_guards.py — unit test for the new guard\n- .github/workflows/release.yml — wire the new guard into the Authorize release source job\n\n## Testing\n- pytest tests/unit/test_release_guards.py tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py -q\n- make lint && make typecheck\n- Non-codebase attestation: re-run release.yml run 33273822041's \"Publish to MCP Registry\" job and\n  record its result URL/timestamp as a ticket comment (not gated by an in-repo AC).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] server.json's top-level description is <= 100 characters.\n- [ ] scripts/release_guards.py exposes check_mcp_registry_description with a passing unit test in\n      tests/unit/test_release_guards.py.\n- [ ] .github/workflows/release.yml's Authorize release source job invokes\n      `release_guards.py mcp-registry-description` as a real guard step (verifiable via\n      `grep mcp-registry-description .github/workflows/release.yml`), so this class of failure is\n      caught before PyPI publish in future releases.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The re-run \"Publish to MCP Registry\" job for release.yml run 33273822041 is\n      confirmed successful and its result URL/timestamp is recorded as a ticket comment.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"server.json","reason":"shorten top-level description field to satisfy the MCP registry <=100 char schema"},{"path":"scripts/release_guards.py","reason":"add check_mcp_registry_description guard + CLI subcommand"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_release_guards.py","reason":"unit test for the new guard"},{"path":".github/workflows/release.yml","reason":"wire the new guard into the Authorize release source job"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f6d32cef-ac77-41d7-b838-9adc00a4f34a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9497-da35-e247-4cb5","ticket_type":"task","title":"server.json top-level description exceeds MCP Registry's 100-char limit, blocking registry publish","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a13b9ddd-d855-4396-9851-960229568976","1bf7cbe6-c624-46ff-a278-d8baffe193cd","2a05427e-b6c4-476c-bfa3-d13f97a1bbfa","1a0159b9-7537-437c-9c30-dfd4a8170d54","b36d2ba1-ef54-4859-bd16-0ac42b74234e","dfe2c0e5-60f0-4fdd-a372-8ac2f0fdf2ca","f6d32cef-ac77-41d7-b838-9adc00a4f34a","7569a4e5-dc51-48f5-b3ad-4332d0ee0b83","2f0696e2-6293-4ad8-9a3f-407eb435be13"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788037527999641002,"uuid":"217387c3-fb37-4af5-b086-29b6e3ee2b1c"}